InterGenOS Authors
==================

This file lists the contributors to InterGenOS — the people whose work
appears in the project's git history — and the AI models whose
co-authorship that history records. It is maintained alongside the
CREDITS file (which lists upstream projects InterGenOS builds upon)
and SOURCES.md (the GPL source-availability commitment).

Order within a section is roughly chronological by first contribution.
Contributors are welcome to amend their entry (preferred name, email,
role) by pull request.

Copyright statement
-------------------

Aggregate copyright on the InterGenOS-authored portion of the
codebase is held jointly by the individuals listed below, under the
terms of GPL-3.0-or-later. See LICENSE for the operative license
text. Per the DCO 1.1 (see DCO.md), each commit's Signed-off-by
trailer attests authorship and right-to-submit for that commit.

Project lead and maintainer
---------------------------

* InterGenJLU
  Operator, maintainer, and project lead since the original
  2015–2016 build cycles (`github.com/InterGenOS/build_001` through
  `build_003`) and the 2026 revival cycle.
  Trades as InterGen Studios <intergenstudios.com>.

Coordinator roles
-----------------

The project uses an AI-coordinator fleet for routine build, audit,
documentation, and verification work. Coordinator commits are
operator-signed (per DCO.md §4) and carry a `Co-Authored-By:` trailer
naming the AI model that produced the change (the record is the "AI
models" section below). Coordinators do not hold independent
authorship for purposes of this AUTHORS file; the operator's
Signed-off-by is the load-bearing contributor record.

* build-system coordinator
  Build VM and chroot pipeline work, mirror/signing infrastructure,
  release engineering. Coordinator role since 2026-03-30.

* installed-system coordinator
  Installed-system hardening, intergen safety architecture, kernel
  and service hygiene. Coordinator role since 2026-04 (approx).

* windows-host coordinator
  Cross-host integration, documentation surfaces, repository trust
  architecture, supply-chain audit. Coordinator role since 2026-04
  (approx).

AI models (the co-authorship record)
------------------------------------

InterGenOS is built with AI-augmented development, and the project
records that fact rather than hiding it. Every change produced with a
model's help carries a `Co-Authored-By:` trailer naming the model,
under the e-mail address its vendor is attributed with on GitHub.
None of these addresses is a linked GitHub account, so GitHub renders
the name as written. The operator's Signed-off-by stays the
load-bearing contributor record (DCO.md §4); the models hold no
copyright and no independent authorship, exactly as the coordinator
roles above.

Each entry below is the trailer exactly as the history carries it —
one line per spelling, in order of first use — followed by its
figures; the entries are in order of first contribution. The "Public"
figures are counted over this repository's `dev` history at its
2026-10-17 tip (1,847 commits, 1,797 of them carrying at least one
model trailer), one count per commit per distinct trailer:

    git log --date=short --format='%x00%ad%x01%B' dev

The "Pre-publication" figures cover the development history of
2026-03-30 to 2026-08-16 (3,775 commits, 3,567 with a model trailer).
That history is not in this repository — the import commit of
2026-08-16 stands for it and names the models that worked in it — so
those figures are stated by the maintainer and cannot be reproduced
from the public tree. "The import commit" means the model's only
public appearance is that commit's trailer list.

